<title>USA: Hilton says Bally chairman to run gaming.</title>
<headline>Hilton says Bally chairman to run gaming.</headline>
<dateline>BEVERLY HILLS, Calif. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hilton Hotels Corp said Tuesday that Bally Entertainment Corp Chairman Arthur Goldberg will run the combined company's gaming operations after the two companies merge.</p>
<p>Earlier Hilton reported net income for its third quarter ended September 30 of $54.5 million, or $0.28 a share compared with $24.8 million, or $0.13 a share in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Those results reflect the company's four-for-one stock split, which was effective September 19.</p>
